The [[States and union territories of India|state]] of '''[[Andhra Pradesh]]''' has 28 [[Districts of India|districts]]. [[Visakhapatnam district]] is the smallest district in area while [[Kadapa district]] is the largest. [[Nellore district]] is the most populous whereas [[Polavaram district]] is the least populous district. The districts are further divided into one, two or more [[revenue division]]s, which are further subdivided into [[List of mandals in Andhra Pradesh|mandals]] for administrative purposes.

== History ==
At the time of [[Partition of India|Independence]] the present day [[Andhra Pradesh]] was a part of the [[Madras State]]. The Telugu speaking dominant regions Kostaandhra and Rayalaseema were separated from Madras State to form [[Andhra State]] in 1953.<ref>{{Cite web|date=1 November 2020|title=History of Andhra Pradesh|url=https://www.thehansindia.com/andhra-pradesh/history-of-andhra-pradesh-have-a-quick-recall-of-formation-of-the-state-654080|url-status=live|access-date=3 April 2022|website=The Hans India|language=en|archive-date=3 April 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220403095807/https://www.thehansindia.com/andhra-pradesh/history-of-andhra-pradesh-have-a-quick-recall-of-formation-of-the-state-654080}}</ref>

As Andhra State, it consisted of 11 districts, which are [[Anantapur district|Anantapur]], [[Chittoor district|Chittoor]], [[East Godavari district|East Godavari]], [[Guntur district|Guntur]], [[Kadapa district|Kadapa]], [[Krishna district|Krishna]], [[Kurnool district|Kurnool]], [[Nellore district|Nellore]], [[Srikakulam district|Srikakulam]], [[Visakhapatnam district|Visakhapatnam]] and [[West Godavari district|West Godavari]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=30 March 2022|title=AP new districts: First formed under the empire, Andhra Pradesh's map shaped and reshaped over two centuries|url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/city/visakhapatnam/first-formed-under-the-empire-aps-map-shaped-and-reshaped-over-two-centuries/articleshow/90528597.cms|access-date=3 April 2022|website=The Times of India|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=2 April 2022|title=New districts in AP: Experts want the government to walk the talk|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/new-districts-in-ap-experts-want-the-government-to-walk-the-talk/article65284435.ece|url-status=live|access-date=3 April 2022|website=The Hindu|language=en |archive-date=3 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220403071546/https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/new-districts-in-ap-experts-want-the-government-to-walk-the-talk/article65284435.ece }}</ref>

As a result of the 1956 [[States Reorganisation Act]], the state's boundaries were re-organized following linguistic lines. On 1 November 1956, the Andhra State and the [[Telangana]] region of the [[Hyderabad State (1948–1956)|Hyderabad State]] were merged to form the Andhra Pradesh which is retrospectively referred to as [[United Andhra Pradesh]].

As united Andhra Pradesh,  it consisted of 21 districts, with 10 districts of Telangana region.{{citation needed|date=March 2023}} In the year 1959, [[Bhadrachalam]] and [[Venkatapuram, Jayashankar Bhupalpally district|Nuguru Venkatapuram]] taluks of [[East Godavari district]], which are on the other side of the [[Godavari River]], were merged into [[Khammam district]] on grounds of geographical contiguity and administrative viability. Similarly [[Aswaraopeta]] part of [[West Godavari District]] was added to [[Khammam district]] and [[Munagala]] taluk belonging to [[Krishna district]] was added to [[Nalgonda district]] in the same year.<ref>{{Cite news |last=ANI |date=2013-11-12 |title=GoM on Andhra bifurcation to elicit views of political parties |work=Business Standard India |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/politics/gom-on-andhra-bifurcation-to-elicit-views-of-political-parties-113111200303_1.html |access-date=2023-03-14}}</ref>

The number of districts became 23 with the formation of [[Prakasam district]]  from the parts of Guntur, Nellore and Kurnool districts in 1970 and [[Vizianagaram district]] from parts of Visakhapatnam and Srikakulam districts in 1979.

After the bifurcation of the United Andhra Pradesh in 2014, the Andhra region now known as [[Andhra Pradesh]] was left with 13 districts but was given several tribal-dominated mandals from the Khammam district of the [[Telangana]] as part of the [[Polavaram Project|Polavaram project]]. These mandals were added to the East Godavari and West Godavari district's respectively.<ref>{{Cite web|date=3 September 2014|title=Andhra Pradesh takes control of seven mandals in Khammam|url=https://www.deccanchronicle.com/140903/nation-current-affairs/article/andhra-pradesh-takes-control-seven-mandals-khammam|access-date=3 April 2022|website=Deccan Chronicle|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=11 July 2014|title=List of seven mandals to be included in AP|url=https://www.thehansindia.com/posts/index/Andhra-Pradesh/2014-07-11/List-of-seven-mandals-to-be-included-in-AP/101564|access-date=3 April 2022|website=The Hans India|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2014-08-19 |title=TS gives up on 7 transferred mandals |language=en-IN |work=The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/./article60389782.ece |access-date=2023-03-14 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2014-07-14 |title=Parliament passes bill on Polavaram project |language=en-IN |work=The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/parliament-passes-bill-on-polavaram-project/article6210089.ece |access-date=2023-03-14 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref>

On 26 January 2022, the [[Government of Andhra Pradesh]] proposed 13 new districts by issuing a draft notification under the Andhra Pradesh Districts (Formation) Act, 1974, Section 3(5).<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-01-31 |title=Doubling the number of districts in Andhra Pradesh: The proposal and the criticism |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/explained/doubling-the-number-of-districts-in-andhra-pradesh-the-proposal-and-the-criticism-7749809/ |access-date=2023-03-11 |website=The Indian Express |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite news|last=Raghavendra|first=V.|date=26 January 2022|title=With creation of 13 new districts, AP now has 26 districts|work=[[The Hindu]]|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/with-creation-of-13-new-districts-ap-now-has-26-districts/article38327788.ece|url-status=live|access-date=26 January 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220126110443/https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/with-creation-of-13-new-districts-ap-now-has-26-districts/article38327788.ece|archive-date=26 January 2022|issn=0971-751X}}</ref> After taking the objections and suggestions received from the public into consideration, the government has published the final notification on 3 April 2022. With effect from 4 April 2022 the newly formed districts came into effect as specified in the schedule.<ref>{{Cite web|date=30 March 2022|title=New districts to come into force on April 4|work=[[The Hindu]]|url=https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/new-districts-to-come-into-force-on-april-4/article65274658.ece|access-date=3 April 2022}}</ref><ref name="apreorg-2022">{{Cite web |url=https://www.sakshipost.com/news/andhrapradesh/heres-how-new-ap-map-looks-after-districts-reorganization-153041 |title=Here's how new ap map looks after districts reorganisation |date=2022-04-03 |access-date=2023-04-17}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=31 March 2022|title=Andhra Pradesh to have 13 new districts from April 4|url=https://www.india.com/news/india/andhra-pradesh-to-have-13-new-districts-from-april-4-check-list-of-total-26-districts-here-5317197/|access-date=3 April 2022|website=[[india.com]]|language=en}}</ref> At present there are 26 districts spread across 3 cultural regions: [[North Andhra|Uttaraandhra]], [[Coastal Andhra|Kostaandhra]] and [[Rayalaseema]].

The government formed [[Markapuram district|Markapuram]] and [[Polavaram district|Polavaram]] districts with effect from 31 December 2025 after receiving proposals from public.By this the districts count is increased from 26 to 28.<ref name="districts-20253112">{{Cite news |title=Andhra News:కొత్త జిల్లాలు పోలవరం, మార్కాపురం |date=2025-12-30 |url=https://www.eenadu.net/telugu-news/andhra-pradesh/ap-cabinet--approves-formation-of-two-new-districts/1799/125240498 |access-date=2026-02-16 |work=Eenadu|language=te}}</ref>

