== Regional development clusters ==
The [[Government of Andhra Pradesh]] has also proposed three new regional development clusters to promote balanced growth across the state. These regions group nearby districts based on geography and economic potential. For instance, the '''Tirupati region''' includes all [[Rayalaseema]] districts such as [[Anantapur district|Ananthapuramu]], [[Sri Sathya Sai district|Sri Sathya Sai]], [[Kurnool district|Kurnool]], [[Nandyal district|Nandyal]], [[Kadapa district|YSR Kadapa]], [[Annamayya district|Annamayya]], [[Chittoor district|Chittoor]], and [[Tirupati district|Tirupati]], along with [[Nellore district|SPSR Nellore]] district. Similarly, the '''Visakhapatnam region''' covers the [[North Andhra|North Coastal]] districts including  [[Alluri Sitharama Raju district|Alluri Sitharama Raju]], [[Anakapalli district|Anakapalli]], [[Parvathipuram Manyam district|Parvathipuram Manyam]], [[Polavaram district|Polavaram]], [[Srikakulam district|Srikakulam]], [[Visakhapatnam district|Visakhapatnam]], [[Vizianagaram district|Vizianagaram]],along with [[Kakinada district|Kakinada]], [[East Godavari district|East Godavari]] and [[West Godavari district|West Godavari]] and The '''Amaravati–Vijayawada region''' includes [[Bapatla district|Bapatla]], [[East Godavari district|East Godavari]], [[Eluru district|Eluru]], [[Guntur district|Guntur]], [[Kakinada district|Kakinada]],[[Konaseema district|Konaseema]], [[Krishna district|Krishna]], [[Markapuram district|Markapuram]], [[NTR district|NTR]], [[Palnadu district|Palnadu]] and [[Prakasam district|Prakasam]]. These regional clusters are aimed at improving infrastructure, industrial development, and administrative coordination across [[Andhra Pradesh]].

